{
  "uid": "takehome-overhead",
  "title": "Integration Overhead",
  "tags": [
    "takehome",
    "comparison"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 99,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard answers",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**A: k6 -> `service/app.py` -> `llm/gemini.py` -> Vertex** \u2014 our integration under external traffic, exactly as production would drive it.\n\n**B: k6 -> Vertex directly** \u2014 the vendor baseline.\n\n**A - B is what our layer costs.** `service_overhead_seconds` measures the same thing from inside the process and excludes the inbound HTTP hop, so it will read lower than the A-B delta; the gap between them is transit and framework cost.\n\nIf throughput plateaus while `service_overhead_seconds` stays flat, the ceiling is the vendor or the outbound pool, not our code."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Throughput: served vs shed",
      "description": "Divergence here is the cost of the Python client.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8
          }
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(service_requests_total{outcome=\"success\"}[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "served",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(service_admission_rejected_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "shed (503)",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Where the time goes",
      "description": "Inbound end-to-end vs upstream vendor time. The gap is ours.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(service_request_duration_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "inbound p99 (total)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(llm_request_duration_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "upstream p99 (vendor)",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(service_overhead_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "our overhead p99",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Admission queue wait",
      "description": "Growth here is the earliest saturation signal, ahead of latency or errors.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(service_queue_wait_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "queue wait p99",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "service_inflight_requests",
          "legendFormat": "inflight",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Generator health (control only)",
      "description": "k6 dropped_iterations must stay at zero. Anything above zero means the generator could not sustain the offered rate, and the control is no longer a valid reference.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(k6_dropped_iterations_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "dropped iterations/s",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(k6_vus)",
          "legendFormat": "active VUs",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rate limiting seen by each harness",
      "description": "If only one harness sees 429s at the same offered rate, quota is being attributed to something other than raw request count.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(llm_retry_attempts_total{reason=\"LLMRateLimitError\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "subject 429/s",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(k6_gemini_rate_limited_total[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "control 429/s",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}